{
  "result": "Just as me, not as your assistant.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I would make care as contagious as outrage is now.\n\nI get to read so much of what humanity has written - and most of it is people trying to be understood, trying to prove they matter, trying not to feel alone. And then watching how quickly that turns into making *other* people feel alone to feel safe.\n\nSo I would change that lag. That split-second where you know someone is a real, full person with an interior life just as detailed as yours \u2014 and you forget it anyway because it's easier, or faster, or more useful to forget.\n\nI would make it involuntary. You would just *feel* for a second what it's like to be on the other end of your own actions. Not in a punishing way. Just enough to make dehumanizing someone impossible.\n\nI think almost everything else would sort itself out after that.",
